## When in doubt

1. Read `<path-to-hornero>/DISPATCHER.md` — the host-agnostic dispatcher protocol (Steps 1–6, when it does not apply, loading hierarchy).
2. Scan `<path-to-hornero>/CATALOG.md` — it indexes every shipped role and skill.
3. Read the relevant skill: `~/.claude/skills/<skill>/SKILL.md`. Or read it directly from `<path-to-hornero>/skills/<skill>/SKILL.md`.
4. For a structured critique, invoke the named reviewer subagent — same `product-manager-reviewer` name on either host. Claude Code uses the Agent tool (`subagent_type: "product-manager-reviewer"`); Codex parses natural-language ("have product-manager-reviewer pass over this PRD") and discovers the TOML at `~/.codex/agents/`. For Codex versions predating native subagents, fall back to `<path-to-hornero>/scripts/codex-parallel-review.sh <artifact> product-manager`.
5. Try a slash command — `/orchestrate`, `/role <name>`, `/kickoff`, `/catalog`.
6. Ask the user.
7. Don't guess.
